
       Delivery Note for Observation - 4297/0931790101 (SN2023ixf)
       ===============================================================

XFTS Delivery Date to SOC : Mon Jul  3 11:05:07 2023

1 PCMS Processing
-----------------

Full release note for ppsprod-20.10
======================================

Pipeline Version: 20.10_20230417_1156
Pipeline name: ppsprod
Release Date: 2023-04-17
SAS Manifest: xmmsas_20220901_1330



Summary
=======
This version of the pipeline is aimed to be inline with latest
public SAS release (SAS20) and to fix a few identified bugs.

Most relevant problem fixed is the wrong values for the effective
area associated to EPIC-pn spectra from exposures in Timing and
Burst modes. These wrong values affected all observations since
September 2017, independently on the SAS or pipeline code version.

An incorrect list of OM processed sources included in the summary
file named PINDEX and with a side effect in the summary html
files has also been fixed.

The version of SAS being used is a pipeline-specific manifest
xmmsas_20220901_1330. This is based on the public SAS release 20.0.0,
described at
http://www.cosmos.esa.int/web/xmm-newton/sas-release-notes-2000



Documentation
=============

Documentation for this pipeline can be found at:

http://www.cosmos.esa.int/web/xmm-newton/pipeline

and links therein.



Pipeline Summary
================

i.   Products created.
ii.  SAS Tasks.
iii. Calibration files.
iv.  Response matrices.
v.   Energy Bands.
vi.  Energy Conversion Factors.
vii. Source Position Rectification.


i. Products Created
===================

The following table summarises all possible product files created by
this pipeline. Withdrawn products are noted for completeness.

Product file names are subdivided into components:

        Pooooooooooiiseeeccccccbnnn.ttt

where:
oooooooooo is the Observation Identifier.
ii         is the instrument.
s          is the scheduled flag.
eee        is the exposure number.
cccccc     is the file identifier given in the table below.
b          is the instrument specific field (ISF):
               Energy band for EPIC instruments.
               OM science window or OM filter code for OM products.
               Spectral order for RGS products.
nnn        is the hexidecimal source number or 000.
ttt        is the file type.



